<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Safras ups soybean crop to 26.89 mln tonnes. [CORRECTED 20:55 GMT]</title>
<headline>Brazil Safras ups soybean crop to 26.89 mln tonnes. [CORRECTED 20:55 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's 1996/97 soybean crop should reach 26.88 (corrects from 26.89) million tonnes, up from a December forecast of 26.28 million tonnes, said independent consultants Safras e Mercado.</p>
<p>The latest forecast compares with an upwardly revised 1995/96 estimate of 24.15 million tonnes. Previously Safras had put the 1995/96 crop at 23.49 million tonnes.</p>
</text>
